            "japan-emperor-cabinet-advice",
            "japan-emperor-enumerated-acts",
            "japan-succession-male-line",
            "japan-practice-influence-question",
          ],
          "traceStatus": "qualified",
        },
        {
          "body": "The consulted 2013 consolidation specifies a Legislative Assembly with seventeen people's representatives and nine nobles' representatives, alongside Cabinet members, but that text alone does not establish a pre-reform comparison or democratic outcome.
An official Crown Law release records that in December 2010 the King appointed Lord Tu'ivakano prime minister on the Assembly's recommendation; the Constitution also specifies retained royal functions.
The consulted English consolidation should not displace Tongan texts and meanings; how missionary and colonial mediation shaped that record remains an explicit research question.",
          "heading": "What changed in Tonga in 2010?",
          "id": "tonga",
